/E (The use of dynamic, psychologically reactive environments, where the setting shifts to mirror the protagonist's internal state. From the warm, fake safety of Camelot to the cold, disorienting wilderness; and, finally to the desolate, grave-like Green Chapel. This established the technique of "atmospheric progression," where weather, lighting, and architecture telegraph emotional shifts and rising dread to the audience. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [5]
>>
